#: ../../source/administration-guide/configure/calls-kubernetes.md:54
msgid "Kubernetes-Specific Configuration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/configure/calls-kubernetes.md:56
msgid "Network Configuration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/configure/calls-kubernetes.md:58
msgid ""
"For Kubernetes deployments, you need to ensure specific connectivity "
"paths:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/configure/calls-kubernetes.md:60
msgid ""
"**Client to RTCD connectivity**: UDP and TCP traffic on port 8443 is "
"properly routed from clients to RTCD pods (for media, with TCP acting as "
"a fallback)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/configure/calls-kubernetes.md:61
msgid ""
"**Mattermost to RTCD API connectivity**: There needs to be a clear "
"connectivity path between Mattermost and RTCD on the API port (TCP 8045)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/configure/calls-kubernetes.md:62
msgid ""
"**Network policies**: Network policies must allow the required "
"communications between Mattermost and RTCD services"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/configure/calls-kubernetes.md:64
msgid "Resource Requirements"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/configure/calls-kubernetes.md:66
msgid ""
"Resource requirements for RTCD pods depend heavily on the expected call "
"volume, participant count, and whether screen sharing is used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/configure/calls-kubernetes.md:68
msgid ""
"We strongly recommend reviewing the [Performance Baselines](calls-"
"metrics-monitoring.md#performance-baselines) to determine the appropriate"
" CPU, memory, and network requests and limits for your specific "
"deployment needs rather than relying on generic defaults."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/configure/calls-kubernetes.md:70
msgid "Scaling Considerations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/configure/calls-kubernetes.md:72
msgid "Horizontal scaling of RTCD pods is possible, but remember:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/configure/calls-kubernetes.md:74
msgid "Each call is hosted entirely on a single RTCD pod"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/configure/calls-kubernetes.md:75
msgid ""
"DNS A records should be set up for all RTCD pods so server can discover "
"RTCD servers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/configure/calls-kubernetes.md:76
msgid "Health checks should ensure that only healthy pods are reported via DNS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/configure/calls-kubernetes.md:77
msgid "Calls remain on their assigned pod for their entire duration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/configure/calls-kubernetes.md:79
msgid "Limitations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/configure/calls-kubernetes.md:81
msgid ""
"Due to the inherent complexities of hosting a WebRTC service, some "
"limitations apply when deploying Calls in a Kubernetes environment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/configure/calls-kubernetes.md:83
msgid ""
"One key requirement is that each `rtcd` process must live in a dedicated "
"Kubernetes node. This is necessary to forward the data correctly while "
"allowing for horizontal scaling. Data should generally direct directly to"
" the pod running the `rtcd` process, as routing this traffic through a "
"standard ingress is not recommended for RTCD deployments."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/configure/calls-kubernetes.md:85
msgid ""
"The general recommendation is to expose one external IP address per "
"`rtcd` instance (Kubernetes node). This makes it simpler to scale as the "
"application is able to detect its own external address (through STUN) and"
" advertise it to clients to achieve connectivity with minimal "
"configuration."
msgstr ""

